Jin was one of the two fey who held court in a glade deep in the [[Verdant Expanse]], and the one who spoke for it. He was tall and gangly with bluish-gray skin, a fused bone mask for a face, and gossamer wrappings. He wore a black raiment.

He was bemused by the investigators and called them dogs of the state. He said the court did not know the man they sought, that names were of little use to the fey, and that plenty passed through their wastes. He said the man they wanted was not there anymore and was happy, and that he had not been husked. He asked which of the three was most attuned to the forest, and said either [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Cedric Corot|Cedric Corot]] or the ten-foot man would make a good gift.

When the investigators attacked, he fought with thorns and confusion magic. He was killed in the glade.
